{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And he divided against them.</b> According to its plain sense, emend the verse to read ״וַיֵּחָלֵק הוּא וַעֲבָדָיו עֲלֵיהֶם לַיְלָה״ — the way pursuers split up after the pursued, when they flee this way and that." "<b>By night.</b> That is to say: after it grew dark, he did not refrain from pursuing them. And its midrash aggadah — that the night was split: in its first half a miracle was done for him, and its second half was preserved and came around for him to divide the night of Egypt." "<b>As far as Chovah.</b> There is no place whose name is Chovah; rather, Dan calls it Chovah, on account of the idolatry that was destined to be there."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:39.175070692Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}